course: dictionary
lesson: 3624
title: Financially and the money side of things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Financially is an adverb. It tells you in what way something is true: it means in a way that is about money. Look at the words around it to be sure. «The family was financially secure, with savings for the winter.» Secure means safe, and savings are money, so financially secure means safe with money.
explain: Sometimes the clue is a joke. «"Financially challenged" is a joking way to say poor or broke.» The word challenged sounds like a sports word, but here the whole phrase is about money trouble. Ask yourself: what is the money side of this sentence?
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap "about money" into the sentence in place of the hard word. «It is a long drive, but about money it makes sense to take the train.» If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Financially means in a way that is about money.
fact: Financially is an adverb, so it tells you in what way something is true.
fact: «Financially secure» means safe with money.
fact: «Struggling financially» means having a hard time with money.
fact: «Financially challenged» is a joking way to say poor or broke, so read the joke in the context.
exercise: «The family was financially secure, with savings for the winter.» What does financially secure mean? | Safe from the rain | *Safe with money | Sure of the way home | Full of food
exercise: «It is a long drive, but financially it makes sense to take the train.» What does financially tell you the point is about? | The speed of the train | *The money side of the choice | The weather on the day | The feelings of the travellers
exercise: Jamie says a broke friend is «financially challenged». What is Jamie's joke? | *A funny way to say broke | Rich and very happy | A sports club for runners | A kind of maths test
test: «Many families are struggling financially after food prices rose.» What does struggling financially mean? | *Having a hard time with money | Swimming against a strong current | Living in a very big house | Running fast in a race
test: Which word means in a way about money? | fantastically | frozen | forward | *financially
exam: «The shop's ideas were fine, but financially it did not work.» What does financially show? | The ideas were very funny | *The point is about money, and the shop lost out | The shop was a long way from home | The shop was very cold
